21: Marine Tube Ahead\nThe Walk-Through Aquarium
22: Zinzolin: Mmm, it's so warm here.\c\nLet me get to the point.\c\nI have papers that\nLord Ghetsis left behind.\c\nWith these, you can read the ancient\nscripts in the Abyssal Ruins.\c\nAs my own small, little way to atone\nfor my sins, I'll read them to you!\c
23: [VAR TRNAME(0)] is now able to read\nthe Abyssal Ruins script!
24: Just to make sure you know,\nyou reach the Abyssal Ruins\r\nby using Dive in Undella Bay.\c\nAnd you must write down the\nciphers you find in the\r\nAbyssal Ruins by yourself.
25: According to Lord Ghetsis's papers,\nthe ancient peoples read in the\r\nopposite direction to how we read now.\c
26: This is what was written\nin the papers...\c\nIf you reach the second floor,\nread by shifting one letter.\c\nIf you reach the third floor,\nread by shifting two letters.\c\nWhat I mean by “shifting" is replacing\na letter with the previous\r\nletter in the alphabet.\c
27: The king must be the presence that\nstopped the war and united the people.\c
28: The king could see the future\nand talk to all living things.\r\nHe united the people.\c\nIf that is the truth,\nhe was just like the hero!\c
29: There are some characters I can't\nrecognize, but based on the context...\c\nAn extremely wonderful king\nwas laid to rest in those ruins.\c\nIf that king has descendants,\nmaybe those special powers\r\nwere passed down...\c
30: What?!\nYou made it even further, you say?\c\nAnd what kind of ciphers were there?\c\n...\n...\c\nAhem... Oh, yes, now I see.\c
31: Keep searching!\c\nYou need to write down the\nAbyssal Ruins ciphers.
32: Now that I've learned everything\nI wanted to know about the\r\nAbyssal Ruins, I take my leave.\c\nYou are my enemy,\nbut your accomplishments and skill\r\nmake you a worthwhile enemy. Adieu!\c
